#chip mega328p, 16

'Repeat For test (Change 1654): If Not Flag with the condition FALSE (variables pre-set before the loop). When a condition is true its body runs uncounted, by design, so the loop runs slightly long.
'Expect: compiles, and the whole Repeat For construct runs exactly 320,000 clock cycles
'(checked by simulating the generated assembly instruction by instruction)

#option explicit
Dim Flag As Bit
Dim Cnt As Byte
Dim Xv As Byte
Dim Yv As Byte
Flag = 1
Xv = 200
Yv = 1
Cnt = 0
Repeat For 20 ms
    If Not Flag Then
        Xv = 1
    End If
End Repeat
Do
Loop
